<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Francis Edward Stuart</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1688">1688</a>–1766</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as the Old Pretender</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Francis Edward Stuart, known as the Old Pretender, was the son of the Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-england">James II of England</a> and the Jacobite claimant to the thrones of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and Ireland. His birth in 1688 helped provoke the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a>, and he was raised in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/act-of-settlement-1701">Act of Settlement</a> excluded him, and the rising of 1715 in his name failed. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-francis-edward-stuart.jpg" alt="James Francis Edward Stuart" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexis Simon Belle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prince_James_Francis_Edward_Stuart_by_Alexis_Simon_Belle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
